      "description": "From 6 April 2027 the income tax rates on savings income rise to 24%, 44% and 49% at the basic, higher and additional rates across the UK, and those on property income to the same rates in England, Wales and Northern Ireland: 2 percentage points above current law, which already includes Budget 2025's rises. Finance cost relief for landlords follows the property basic rate, so rises to 24%. Dividend rates are unchanged. Incomes are held fixed, with no behavioural response.",
